<p>Two different jobs live in <code>pop-crypt</code>. Hashing is one-way: you store a password hash and later check a
guess against it. Encryption is two-way: you protect a value you need to read back. Passwords always take
the first path; card numbers, API tokens and anything you hand back to a service take the second.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
